  "worked_solution": "Here, the denominator is the imaginary number $3\\text{i}.$ Note that this can be written as $0+3\\text{i},$ so the conjugate is $0-3\\text{i},$ or simply $-3\\text{i}.$\n\nSo, we multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-3\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6-4\\text{i}}{3\\text{i}} & =\\frac{6-4\\text{i}}{3\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-3\\text{i}}{-3\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-18\\text{i}+12{\\text{i}}^{2}}{-9{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-18\\text{i}+12(-1)}{-9(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-12-18\\text{i}}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-12-18\\text{i}}{9} & =-\\frac{12}{9}-\\frac{18}{9}\\text{i} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{3}-2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
